module tasks.`2026-11-23-svg-loop-fresh-checkout`

task SvgLoopFreshCheckout {
  title "make svg-loop fails on a fresh checkout: phase-a-inspected.json is read but never written"
  verify $ make svg-loop
  paths "crates/bboxy450-svg", "Makefile"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add; report what you removed.

    ## Evidence (2026-11-23, Oracle Vesper Greywind)
    - Fresh worktree `~/mydev/bbx-live-checks` at origin/main debec2374: `make svg-loop` exit 2.
      Chrome/158.0.8127.37 pinned, 81 runs, unit tests OK, then
      `crates/bboxy450-svg/review.py:130` raises FileNotFoundError on `target/svg-loop/phase-a-inspected.json`.
    - No source writes that file; `git log -S phase-a-inspected` shows only d949b0eb8, which added the reader.
      The gate passes only in a target dir that still holds an earlier, hand-made inspection record.

    ## Do
    Make the gate unattended and reproducible from a clean checkout. Either produce the inspection record
    from a checked step inside `make svg-loop` (a script that inspects the actual images and writes the digests),
    or keep the reviewed record as a tracked fixture beside `fixtures/advisories.json` and check its digests
    against the current images. Missing or stale inspection must still fail. Add a negative control:
    a changed image with an unchanged record must fail. Run `make svg-loop` twice in a fresh worktree; both exit 0.
    Name what you removed.

    ## Report from seat:01M85H7DD9CN50JD4YTGQ6VVFV

    [[Implement]] `make svg-loop` passed twice and generated both PNG inspection records. The gate checks dimensions, diff counts and exact SHA-256 coverage. The changed-image control refused the old record. Removed the hand-seeded inspection dependency and a duplicate reference review. Standalone native verification, licenses and formal parity across 1,000 models passed. The first cold attempt hit the existing Chrome order check on one isolated heatmap capture. The signed worktree is clean.

    ```json
    {
      "op_id": "01M85K7VZ953H7TT7ZGYRFN1YE",
      "commit": "9284782ed77622f2ed832d966572bb8e7acde98b",
      "report": "[[reports/2026-11-23-svg-loop-fresh-checkout.den]]",
      "verify_result": {
        "command": "make svg-loop",
        "exit_code": 0,
        "evidence": [
          {
            "criterion": "Two unattended full SVG loop passes in the assigned worktree",
            "reference": "target/svg-loop-verify-2.log and target/svg-loop-verify-3.log"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Both stages generate and validate exact PNG receipts",
            "reference": "target/svg-fresh-verify/svg-loop/phase-a-inspected.json and target/svg-fresh-verify/svg-loop/native-inspected.json"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Changed PNG with an unchanged record fails",
            "reference": "crates/bboxy450-svg/test_corpus.py:31, exercised in both passing SVG loop logs"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Formal parity on signed source",
            "reference": "target/svg-loop-evidence/test-formal.log, evidence SHA-256 6e6cd4cf0872d3a94e31410ce4e08d8ec6722fce312536c175d290d56fbb1746"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
    ```


    ## Report from seat:01M85H7DD9CN50JD4YTGQ6VVFV

    [[Implement]] Three consecutive fresh-capture `make svg-loop` runs exited 0, with 216 native captures and zero failures each. The shared comparator limits Chrome-only drift to 0.005% of pixels above channel tolerance and normalized mean error of 0.00001. The Oracle's two archived variants passed against the original pinned PNGs. A 100-pixel change was refused with freshly regenerated comparison and inspection evidence. Removed the byte-equality-only Chrome gate and the unsuccessful whole-tile flag. License checks and source-bound formal verification passed. Worktree clean.

    ```json
    {
      "op_id": "01M85MZ55S4YH84R1CJ93N03J8",
      "commit": "5c99ac392055adb16908c74d83d3d14a9617db09",
      "report": "[[reports/2026-11-23-svg-loop-chrome-noise.den]]",
      "verify_result": {
        "command": "make svg-loop",
        "exit_code": 0,
        "evidence": [
          {
            "criterion": "Three consecutive full passes with newly generated Chrome and order-control captures",
            "reference": "target/svg-noise-probe/bounded-{1,2,3}/make.log and exit-code"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Reported Matplotlib variants pass within the stated bounds and larger changes fail",
            "reference": "target/svg-noise-probe/archived-drift.log"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Retain strict SHA-256 inspection and frozen resvg pins",
            "reference": "crates/bboxy450-svg/review.py:59 and :163; target/svg-noise-probe/bounded-3/result.json"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "Formal verification on signed source",
            "reference": "target/svg-noise-probe/test-formal.log, d31aaba2dfc4ffe0f0c135aa08e7789cb1bdcf30130489d598b2000eaa809ba2"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
    ```
    """

